# CORR-8 (main 09-27): ORDER BY key columns whose sort peers display apart (a nondeterministic collation's zz / Zz, numeric
# 1.5 / 1.500) take eqo classes under the sort's `=` (the rig asks PG): tie runs and the key sequence compare by class, rows exactly
# numeric peers 1.5 / 1.500 in one run, their order swapped: ordered by class; each row keeps its own display
sql: SELECT n, id FROM t ORDER BY n;
cols: n	id
eqo: 1	1.5	1.5
eqo: 1	1.500	1.5
eqo: 1	2	2
class: ordered 1
verdict: match
[pg]
1.5	1
1.500	2
2	3
[got]
1.500	2
1.5	1
2	3
